#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-

"""
RAMAN PLS – STANDALONE GUI
==========================

This file contains:
- embedded trained PLS model (no external model file required)
- Raman-CSV-Import
- automatic grouping of repeated measurements
- preprocessing
- PLS1 evaluation
- folder drag and drop
- separate spectra and concentration plots
- UV-Vis NADH concentration calculation from embedded calibration data
- concentration table
- automatic export of numerical results as CSV and JSON
- manual export of plots as high-resolution PNG or SVG

Processing sequence for Raman data:
1. Decode and validate the embedded trained model.
2. Read each CSV and interpolate it onto the model's Raman axis.
3. Remove spikes and apply the exact preprocessing stored with each model.
4. Predict each analyte with its analyte-specific PLS1 model.
5. For repeated measurements, predict every replicate separately and calculate
   the mean concentration and sample standard deviation.
6. Exclude predictions outside each calibration range (NaN); preserve zero and time slots.
7. Show results in the table and plots; save figures only after a button click.

Start in VS Code:
1. Open this file in VS Code.
2. Click "Run Python File" in the top right.
3. Missing Python packages are installed automatically on first start.
4. Separate Raman and UV-Vis GUI windows open immediately.
5. Drag a folder with CSV files into the drop zone or use "Select folder".

Note:
Tkinter is included in many Python installations. If "tkinter" is missing
on macOS, install Python from python.org.
The trained model and UV-Vis calibration are embedded in this file.
Only new measurement CSV files and installed Python packages are required.
"""

